IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cr2-age-and-identity`

-- Tests of cr2-age-and-identity.l4 (regulations 47 to 51). Layer 1.
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the regulations before the rules were run.

§ `Tests -- regulations 47 to 51`

§§ `47 -- determining age and identity`

-- 47(1): arguments: a birth certificate (or copy, or act of birth) is available; the Commission makes information available.
#ASSERT `reg 47(1) — the Minister must determine the person's age and identity on the basis of a document or information in subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 47(1) — the Minister must determine the person's age and identity on the basis of a document or information in subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 47(1) — the Minister must determine the person's age and identity on the basis of a document or information in subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 47(1) — the Minister must determine the person's age and identity on the basis of a document or information in subsection (1)` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 47(2) — the Minister may require the original birth certificate or a copy of the act of birth issued by the competent authority` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 47(2) — the Minister may require the original birth certificate or a copy of the act of birth issued by the competent authority` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 47(3) — the Minister may determine the person's age and identity on the basis of any other information or evidence` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 47(3) — the Minister may determine the person's age and identity on the basis of any other information or evidence` FALSE)
-- 47(4): arguments: unable under (1) to (3); possible to determine from Statistics Canada information.
#ASSERT `reg 47(4) — the Minister may determine the person's age and identity on the basis of information obtained from Statistics Canada` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 47(4) — the Minister may determine the person's age and identity on the basis of information obtained from Statistics Canada` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 47(4) — the Minister may determine the person's age and identity on the basis of information obtained from Statistics Canada` FALSE TRUE)

§§ `49 and 50 -- accepting an age determined elsewhere, and redetermining`

#ASSERT `reg 49 — the Minister may accept the determination of the person's age for the purposes of the Act` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 49 — the Minister may accept the determination of the person's age for the purposes of the Act` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 49 — the Minister may accept the determination of the person's age for the purposes of the Act` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 50 — the Minister may make a new determination of the age of the person` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 50 — the Minister may make a new determination of the age of the person` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 50 — the Minister may make a new determination of the age of the person` FALSE TRUE)

§§ `51 -- requests to Statistics Canada, and disclosure of what they return`

-- Arguments: prescribed form; signed consent; information for a proper search.
#ASSERT `reg 51(a) — a request to Statistics Canada meets the prescribed conditions` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 51(a) — a request to Statistics Canada meets the prescribed conditions` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 51(a) — a request to Statistics Canada meets the prescribed conditions` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 51(a) — a request to Statistics Canada meets the prescribed conditions` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Arguments: the recipient is an officer, clerk or employee of the Department; disclosure is required by a section 105 agreement.
#ASSERT `reg 51(b) — information obtained from Statistics Canada may be disclosed to a person` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 51(b) — information obtained from Statistics Canada may be disclosed to a person` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 51(b) — information obtained from Statistics Canada may be disclosed to a person` FALSE FALSE)
